   "unmapped": [
    "Nonstationarity is general: the whole sequence of per-round reward distributions (nu_{t,a}) is drawn from a known prior; not restricted to a number of switches or variation budget. Complexity measured by the entropy of the optimal-arm sequence H([A*_1,...,A*_n])."
   ],
   "definition_quote": "We model the non-stationary environment by a random variable \\(\\nu\\) drawn from a prior distribution known to the learner. Here \\(\\nu = (\\nu_{t,a})_{t \\in [n], a \\in \\mathcal{A}}\\) ... Regret(\\pi,n) = E[sum_t R_{t,A_t^*} - R_{t,A_t}] ... There exists a constant \\(\\sigma\\), such that for all a, conditioned on F_t, R_{t,a} - E[R_{t,a}|F_t] is sigma sub-Gaussian. And we assume sigma is known to the learner."
  }
